  "summary": "dora is a CLI that turns a SCIP index into a queryable SQLite database, giving AI agents structured answers about a codebase instead of grepping files and reading imports. The tool has two layers: a SCIP layer that runs a configured indexer, parses the resulting protobuf, and loads symbols, references, and file dependencies into SQLite; and a tree-sitter layer that parses source on demand via WebAssembly grammars for things SCIP doesn't cover. Evidence coverage: 199 of 319 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
  "superseded_claim_ids": []
